   "text": {
    "title": {
     "en": "Getting Things Done setup"
    },
    "summary": {
     "en": "Contexts, a waiting-for list and a someday list, ready for the GTD method in a few minutes."
    },
    "description": {
     "en": "Getting Things Done works with any tool that has an inbox, contexts and lists. In OpenTodo, contexts are [labels](https://open-todo.app/docs/labels-and-filters/) and each list is a saved filter.\n\nThe template creates the [labels](https://open-todo.app/docs/labels-and-filters/) `@home`, `@computer`, `@phone`, `@errand`, `@waiting` and `@someday`, a GTD project with sections for next actions, waiting-for and someday, and a weekly reminder to check every project for a next action.\n\nCreate views like `@phone & !@waiting` for the moments you have only your phone. [Saved views](https://open-todo.app/docs/views/) can be pinned to the sidebar with live counts."
    },
    "howToUse": [
     {
      "en": "Start the template; it creates the labels, the GTD project and its sections."
     },
     {
      "en": "Save the views the guide suggests, such as `@phone & !@waiting`, and pin them to the sidebar."
     },
     {
      "en": "Every Friday, the review task asks you to check each project for a next action."
     }
    ],
    "makeItYours": [
     {
      "en": "Rename the contexts to the places you actually work: `@office`, `@workshop`, `@town`."
     },
     {
      "en": "Delete the sections you do not use; a smaller system is one you keep."
     },
     {
      "en": "Give the review task a time that fits your week."
     }
    ]
   },
