   "text": {
    "title": {
     "en": "Weekly review"
    },
    "summary": {
     "en": "A thirty-minute Friday ritual that empties your inboxes, looks back at the week and plans the next one."
    },
    "description": {
     "en": "A weekly review keeps a task list trustworthy. Once a week you get everything out of your head, look at what happened, and decide what matters next.\n\nThis template gives you a project with three sections that repeat [every Friday](https://open-todo.app/docs/recurrence/). Each task carries a small estimate, so the whole review fits in about thirty minutes on the [Day and Week calendars](https://open-todo.app/docs/time-blocking/).\n\nPair it with a saved view such as `@review & due <= today`, pinned to the sidebar, and you have a review dashboard in one click. The [filters guide](https://open-todo.app/docs/filters/) explains the query language."
    },
    "howToUse": [
     {
      "en": "Start the template; the review repeats every Friday with small estimates, about thirty minutes in all."
     },
     {
      "en": "Save a view `@review & due <= today` and pin it: on Friday it is your checklist."
     },
     {
      "en": "Work through the three sections in order: get clear, look back, look ahead."
     }
    ],
    "makeItYours": [
     {
      "en": "Move it to the day your week actually ends."
     },
     {
      "en": "Add your own inboxes to the first section: a notebook, a chat app, a desk drawer."
     },
     {
      "en": "Cut anything that does not earn its minutes after a month."
     }
    ]
   },
